codemap 9
tour gui-widgets
kind layer
author ai
group gui
note The widgets the GUI is written in: methods on Frame in widgets.rs and widgets/code.rs, the text field's state in field.rs, and clipping, the list filter's Needle and counted nouns in text.rs. There is no widget library under this: each widget opens an element or two with the theme's layout and colours, reads what the element tree says the mouse did to that id last frame, and returns the Interaction; the view that called it decides what Action to push. A widget never changes the Model. They exist because the same three lines were being written everywhere, not because anything needed abstracting, so a view that wants something else opens elements through Frame directly. Every clickable widget takes a Target from ids, so its element id is the name a script clicks it by. The only widget with state is the text field, since a caret and a history cannot be derived from anything.

