note The keys a field understands, as Edits from keys::edits: deletes and moves by character or, with alt or ctrl, by word; moves to the row's ends and, with ctrl, the text's ends; shift makes any move extend the selection. Up and down move by row in a field of many lines and recall the history in a field of one. Enter submits, except in a field of many lines, where it breaks the line and ctrl+enter submits (FieldShape::breaks). Ctrl+a selects all, ctrl+u clears, escape drops the keyboard. Ctrl+c and ctrl+x hand the selection out as a ClipboardRequest for the platform to copy, ctrl+v asks it to paste, and the pasted text comes back next frame as typed text. A field that keeps its text on enter (AfterSubmit::Keep) selects it all so the next entry replaces it; one that clears (the Console, the view picker's search) empties.

